[h1]雇佣兵战术套装 / Mercenary Tactical Loadout[/h1]

升级原版背包、爱丽丝背带、皮带与军用护具，增加 [b]17 个挂载位、13 个独立口袋（合计容量81）和1个钥匙容器（容量10）[/b]。独立格子方便分类存放工具、医疗用品和弹药；挂载箱包另有原本的容量。

[h2]用哪些装备升级？[/h2]
背包：大登山包（含旅行款）、军用行李袋、大型背包、军用背包（含军绿、沙漠迷彩与生存者款）。背带：爱丽丝背带普通、绿色、迷彩款。皮带：原版皮带。护臂、护腿、护胫：仅支持[b]军用防弹款[/b]，左右均可升级。

[h2]六类装备[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]背包[/b]：3个口袋（5+15+15）；7个独立挂位，分别挂水壶、急救箱、工具箱、面具、提灯、电子设备和普通尺寸玩偶。
[*][b]背带[/b]：子弹袋、霰弹袋各容量5，提供对应装填加速；两肩各增加1个手枪位。
[*][b]皮带[/b]：左右口袋各容量3，钥匙容器容量10；两个枪位支持同时挂2把兼容长枪，也能搭配手枪；两个通用挂环支持兼容工具、近战武器、对讲机和无绳电话。
[*][b]护臂[/b]：左右各1个容量5的口袋。
[*][b]护腿[/b]：左右各2个容量5的口袋和1个手枪位。
[*][b]护胫[/b]：左右各1个兼容刀具挂位。
[/list]

[h2]挂载与取用[/h2]
水壶位支持兼容水瓶、水壶和烧瓶；箱包位支持普通、专业和兼容医疗包/工具箱；面具位支持防毒、呼吸器、NBC、焊工、万圣节、曲棍球及骨制面具，不含口罩、面巾和头套。提灯位支持兼容油灯、丙烷灯和自制电灯；电子位支持CD机、收音机和对讲机；玩偶挂在背包右侧。

[b]背包可同时挂工具箱和急救箱，使用其中物品时不用先手动取出。[/b]原版操作会按需取用或转移；也可直接从挂载箱拖到兼容快捷槽。

快捷栏与手柄轮盘可取出电子设备到副手并打开原版面板，再次操作收起面板并挂回；电源和播放由设备面板控制。挂载后可继续显示CD字幕、接收广播，效果遵循原版规则。多盏挂载灯可在轮盘分别开关。

[h2]升级与设置[/h2]
[list]
[*]右键兼容装备查看材料、工具和技能需求；可从可访问容器自动取出装备再升级。
[*]安装钥匙容器需要3个兼容钥匙圈，三个都必须为空；容器使用原版钥匙识别逻辑。
[*]独立口袋可通过容器侧栏及“移动到”使用；装备穿戴、落地或放入可访问容器时均可查看。军用护具可换左右侧并保留升级与物品。
[*]六类部件分别设启用开关。关闭会拆除升级与挂件，口袋及内容保留为独立容器，材料不返还。
[*]“背包口袋负重倍率”支持100%、75%、50%、25%、10%、5%，按原版计重结果缩放战术装备本身、背包/背带内容、安装口袋和钥匙容器；普通挂载物品仍按原版计算。
[/list]

[h2]English[/h2]
Upgrade vanilla backpacks, ALICE webbing, belts and military armor with [b]17 attachment slots, 13 separate pouches (81 total capacity), and one key container (capacity10)[/b]. Separate compartments help organize tools, medical supplies and ammunition. Mounted kits retain their own storage capacity.

[list]
[*][b]Backpack[/b]: three pouches (5+15+15), plus seven separate mounts for a water container, first-aid kit, toolbox, mask, lantern, electronic device and regular-size plush toy.
[*][b]Webbing[/b]: a bullet pouch and shotgun-shell pouch (5 each) with corresponding reload bonuses; one additional pistol slot on each shoulder.
[*][b]Belt[/b]: two pouches (3 each), a key container (10), two gun slots supporting two compatible long guns or pistol combinations, and two utility hooks for supported tools, melee weapons, walkie-talkies and cordless phones.
[*][b]Arm guards[/b]: one pouch (5) on each side.
[*][b]Thigh guards[/b]: two pouches (5 each) and one pistol slot on each side.
[*][b]Greaves[/b]: one compatible blade slot on each side.
[/list]

[h2]Mounts and access[/h2]
Supports compatible bottles/canteens/flasks, standard and specialist toolboxes/medical kits, gas masks/respirators/NBC/welding/Halloween/hockey/bone masks, oil/propane/crafted electric lanterns, CD players/radios/walkie-talkies, and regular-size plush toys on the pack's right side. Surgical masks, face wraps and balaclavas are excluded.

[b]Carry a toolbox and first-aid kit together and use their contents without manually unpacking them first.[/b] Supported vanilla actions retrieve or transfer supplies as needed; tools can also be dragged directly to compatible hotbar slots.

Hotbar and controller wheel actions equip electronic devices in the secondary hand and open the native panel; activate again to close it and stow the device. Power/playback remain manual device controls. Mounted devices can continue CD subtitles and radio reception; effects follow vanilla rules. Multiple mounted lights have separate wheel controls.

[h2]Which items can be upgraded?[/h2]
Big Hiking Backpacks (including travel variants), the supported military Duffel Bag, Military/Large Backpacks (including army, desert-camo and survivor variants); standard/green/camo ALICE Belt and Suspenders; the vanilla Belt; and [b]military bulletproof forearm, thigh and shin armor[/b], both sides.

[h2]Upgrades and settings[/h2]
[list]
[*]Right-click supported equipment for material, tool and skill requirements. Upgrading can retrieve equipment from an accessible container.
[*]The key-container upgrade requires three supported key rings, all empty. It uses native key recognition.
[*]Use the container sidebar or Move To for installed pouches, including when equipment is worn, on the ground or in an accessible container. Military armor can swap sides while retaining upgrades and contents.
[*]Each component has an enable option. Disabling removes upgrades and attachments; pouches and contents remain separate containers, without material refunds.
[*]Backpack and pocket weight multiplier:100/75/50/25/10/5 percent of vanilla-counted burden for tactical equipment itself, backpack/webbing contents, installed pouches and the key container. Ordinary attached items retain vanilla weight.
[/list]

